+# After hours subscription hero
+
+`freebuff-pro-after-hours.webp` is the selected COD-486 artwork for Desktop
+Showcase and Spotlight. The copy is rendered by the clients, not embedded in
+the picture. The three subscription variations reuse the active house
+campaign's approved wording, verified read-only on 2026-09-10: Keep building,
+Code anywhere, and Pick your model. The entry price remains catalog-derived.
+
+Generated with the built-in imagegen tool from the third After hours concept:
+cozy late-night maker desk, amber lamp, leafy plant, blank books and notebook,
+ceramic mug and laptop. The approved final edit replaces the laptop wallpaper
+with a perspective-matched screenshot of the actual Freebuff Desktop dark UI.
+The rest of the desk scene is preserved; no promotional text is overlaid.
+Exported to WebP at quality 90 without cropping or resizing. The final PNG and
+edit prompt are retained in the originating task and COD-486 attachment.
+
+The old PNG/SVG artwork is retained for historical reference. The seed now
+uses this WebP. Existing production creative rows do not change on deployment:
+they hold uploaded hero references. The broad seed adds missing copy and does
+not retire old variations, so it must not be used as a production refresh.
+Use an explicitly scoped, reviewed creative refresh while the campaign is
+paused, retain rollback references and verify the served image before activation.
+
+Intermission is excluded. Enabling the global placement experiments is a
+separate operation from refreshing this campaign, and may admit other eligible
+inventory. Confirm current targets, copy, exposure policy and inventory before
+changing those switches.
+
+The Spotlight and Showcase actions follow the current Desktop mint palette.
+This CSS is bundled in Desktop: refreshed campaign images and copy do not update
+installed clients' button styling. Verify a release containing this change before
+claiming the refreshed component treatment is live.
